  "tag": "trial-20261101-mod4-e0-cad-mean-output-independent-copy-repair225",
  "title": "Create an independently bound E0 action-head repair copy and test original-guard physical regressions",
  "kind": "repair",
  "recorded_at": "2026-10-31T23:05:13.563563+00:00",
  "repair_or_experiment_note": "Created an independent E0 action-head repair copy after proving actual SDK scales, CAD stops and optimizer parameter identity. The copy changes only the left crank output/STD and matching Adam rows; the frozen E0 and unrepaired branch remain untouched. All 17 optimizer steps/LR, other actor rows, trunk and critic are retained. Same-input processed mean targets match the original action chain, while action-history feedback and sampled behavior may differ.\n\nCPU readback found 259 finite tensors. A new original-guard physical regression ran four separate first episodes (standing, forward, reverse, literal Fudan JUMP), each 500 controls/10s, totaling 16,000 physics callbacks. All original termination flags remained false. Ground action channels did not exceed six. Jump produced nine sampled bilateral wheel-air runs, with partial nonwheel contacts and substantial heading/tracking error; this is not stable whole-body jumping or 270mm completion. No PPO, optimizer or budget writes occurred.\n\nPreserves original metadata float-adapter error, wrapper-origin false, local source-generation errors, pre-use SHA correction, actual action closure proof, full UTF8 receipts and source-only W35227 A/B/C preparation. Binary models/NPZs remain producer-metadata-only. 227D source is pending and excluded from this frozen scope. The original Fudan rewards, own400N50DR, CAD geometry and original 2mm guards are unchanged. No automatic next three-hour E0 run is selected.\n",
  "validation": "Actual SDK action closure and optimizer identity; 259-finite-tensor independent copy with same-input mean target equivalence; four bounded physical regression purposes and all original failures; W35 continuation source only unless separately admitted; preserve 1506 old tag objects and peels",
